1
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,240
Tokyo, Hong Kong, Singapore.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,660
So the Indian leg of our
journey is finally upon us.

3
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,720
But, well, I'm a little bit worried.

4
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:21,877
I mean, is there anywhere
to get a cheeseburger there?

5
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:25,457
I've always heard India was a land
of curry, disease, too many people.

6
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,370
I know.

7
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:29,946
I'm worried my stomach won't be
able to handle the culture gap.

8
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,360
That assessment is rather distorted.

9
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:33,719
You needn't worry.

10
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,440
It's a country of extraordinary people.

11
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,880
That I assure you, my friends.

12
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,500
Well, we've reached Calcutta.

13
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:44,681
Let's get going.

14
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,249
Let me carry that for you.

15
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:52,750
Want a tattoo?

16
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:53,978
You're very pretty.

17
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,897
Need some antivenom?

18
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:56,977
It won't hurt your stomach.

19
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,119
Stay at our hotel.

20
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,261
Calcutta, India.

21
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:03,580
In the 20th century, its
population is 11 million.

22
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:08,957
Calcutta buzzes with a bustling energy
that will pull you in and never let you go.

23
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:09,957
I don't need any.

24
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,057
I'm sending some cow shit.

25
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,117
Seriously, thank you.

26
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,030
Oh, crap.

27
00:01:13,113 --> 00:01:15,057
Somebody's already stolen my wallet.

28
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:16,437
Tip, tip, tip.

29
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:19,137
If you don't give me tips,
you won't go to heaven, sir.

30
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:22,044
Hey, kid, don't put your
nose all over my stuff.

31
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,440
Avdol, so this is India?

32
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:25,970
See?

33
00:01:26,053 --> 00:01:27,272
Great country, isn't it?

34
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,604
They're what makes India
great, don't you think?

35
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,580
Thank you.

36
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,730
Yeah!

37
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,220
Here, try this.

38
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:10,980
This is chai.

39
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,297
I think you'll find it to your liking.

40
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:15,860
Chai, one of India's most popular drinks.

41
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:20,473
A sweet concoction made by boiling
black tea, sugar, and ginger with milk.

42
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,160
Ah, at last a little piece.

43
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,577
Be patient with India.

44
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:28,542
Once you get used to it, you'll
see how wonderful this country is.

45
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,657
You know, I kind of like this place.

46
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:31,570
It's pretty cool.

47
00:03:31,653 --> 00:03:32,483
What, Jotaro?

48
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,400
You cannot be serious!

49
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,917
It's a hell of a lot of
culture shock, though.

50
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,706
Guess I'll like it once
I get used to it, huh?

51
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:46,089
Well, I guess people adapt to
their surroundings eventually.

52
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,880
Where's the John?

53
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,568
It's right over there, sir.

54
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,000
Polnareff! Yeah?

55
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,897
Aren't you going to order first?

56
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,000
Pick for me.

57
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,064
It better be something amazing.

58
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:01,415
Something gorgeous and sophisticated
that suits a Frenchman such as moi.

59
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:04,517
Which means it doesn't matter.

60
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,718
He'll eat anything.

61
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:06,900
Let's see.

62
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,687
What's something he'll like?

63
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:09,640
Excuse me.

64
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,300
Pardon me, sir.

65
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,774
Could you please wait?

66
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,350
Huh?

67
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:20,615
Please, use this while you're in here.

68
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,920
What am I supposed to do with this? Hey!

69
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,460
Ooh la la!

70
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:36,980
I must say,

71
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:40,937
the toilet looks weird, but at least
it's a lot cleaner than I had expected.

72
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:43,557
A gentleman like myself
has certain standards

73
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:46,464
and won't stand for it
when a bathroom is dirty.

74
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,920
Sir, is something wrong?

75
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:01,910
Don't!

76
00:05:01,993 --> 00:05:03,360
Is something wrong me?

77
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,340
The toilet!

78
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,640
The toilet!

79
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,700
There's a pig sticking its head out of it!

80
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:16,560
Why, yes.

81
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,817
No need to be frightened.

82
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:18,917
He's actually quite friendly.

83
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,057
The builders constructed the pig pen down
below higher than they were supposed to.

84
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:26,017
So, when the pigs get hungry,
they come up for more.

85
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:26,930
That's all.

86
00:05:27,013 --> 00:05:28,597
But that's not even what
I'm asking you about!

87
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,100
No, wait, what?

88
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:33,700
So you're telling me that
this pig's food is...

89
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,888
That's what it's there for?

90
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:38,360
As I told you, sir.

91
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,040
Here, use this stick.

92
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,510
Like this.

93
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:47,057
See, now you can do your business
while the pig's knocked down.

94
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,669
Though, some like the pig.

95
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,865
Our manager gets the pig to lick his
buttocks and always sings the pig's praises.

96
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,840
He gets it so clean.

97
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,147
Feel free to take your time.

98
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:04,250
Hey, monsieur!

99
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,595
Don't leave me alone!

100
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:13,395
I don't think I could ever get used
to this, no matter how much I tried.

101
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,238
I'll wait until we get to the hotel.

102
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,109
Sorry to keep you waiting.

103
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,260
Oh, crap, the food.

104
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:38,680
Where is he?

105
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,330
No way.

106
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,400
Too weird.

107
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:43,620
I know I saw someone out there.

108
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,080
I must have imagined it.

109
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,692
I guess I can't help it.

110
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,897
I mean, there was a pig in
the john, for God's sake.

111
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:54,580
Oh, well, nothing there.

112
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,647
What's a little monster
in the mirror anyway?

113
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:01,604
So this is what they mean
by culture shock here.

114
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,857
What the hell

115
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:21,740
is going on here?

116
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,767
I can only see this damn
thing in the mirror.

117
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:28,940
This must be the mirror
stand Jotaro talked about.

118
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,200
Merde, this is not good.

119
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,320
Mon dieu, this is so not good.

120
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,100
THAT NEW MATERION!

121
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,190
Huh?

122
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,860
Where did that bastard go?

123
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,340
Damn it!

124
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,020
A stand! Huh?

125
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,280
But where's the user? Who is it?

126
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,380
The man with two right hands!

127
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,621
Too many people!

128
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,950
Damn it.

129
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,377
What's the matter, Polnareff?

130
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:11,578
What is this about?

131
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,060
If that was it,

132
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:16,920
If that stand belongs
to who I think it does,

133
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:21,060
then that means I finally found him.

134
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:25,340
Jotaro, the stand user who
uses the mirrors, he's here.

135
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:30,460
The bastard who killed my
sister, my angelic sister.

136
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:36,537
The scum who heartlessly
trampled my sister's life,

137
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:39,457
soul and pride who destroyed the world's

138
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:44,197
most pure heart finally finally we meet?

139
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:50,800
are you absolutely sure
it's him it's settled mr.

140
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:55,997
Joestar I'll be traveling on
My own from here on out with

141
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:59,917
my sister's murderer finally
within reach I'll be Damned

142
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,437
if I'm going to wait for him
to come after me I'm screwed

143
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,417
if he gets that drop on me
and that's just not my style.

144
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:08,441
I'll find him first and kill him!

145
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,957
But we don't even know what he
looks like or what his stand is.

146
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,805
He's got two right hands,
that's enough for me.

147
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:18,260
And don't forget, he knows
that I'm coming after him.

148
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:22,166
That should put him on the
defensive and give me the advantage.

149
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:23,450
See ya.

150
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,402
Tough talk for a man who's
digging his own grave.

151
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:29,920
And that means?

152
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:32,380
Just as it sounds, my friend.

153
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:35,700
Are you implying that I'm going to lose?

154
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,350
Yes.

155
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:38,263
Can't you see?

156
00:09:38,346 --> 00:09:39,857
The enemy attacked in
order to isolate you.

157
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:41,817
He's exploiting your biggest weakness.

158
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:44,200
I won't let you go alone, Polnareff.

159
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,030
Listen up.

160
00:09:46,113 --> 00:09:47,657
I'm only going to say it once.

161
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:50,800
This whole time, I never
once gave a damn about Dio.

162
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,537
I told you in Hong Kong that I would go

163
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:56,326
along with you so that
I could get my revenge.

164
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:57,530
Mr.

165
00:09:57,613 --> 00:09:59,700
Joestar and Jotaro already know this.

166
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,073
Hmm, I've been alone from the beginning.

167
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,977
I've always been fighting alone.

168
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,220
You selfish fool!

169
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,057
Did you forget that you
were brainwashed by Dio?

170
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:12,077
Are you so foolish you forgot
that he's the root of all of this?

171
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:16,417
You have no idea how it feels to have
your sister murdered, so shut the hell up!

172
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:20,760
I heard the last time you met Dio,
you pissed yourself and ran away!

173
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:25,340
A coward like you would never
understand why I need to do this!

174
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,720
What did you say?

175
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,297
Don't touch me!

176
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:31,440
You just got lucky the day
you beat me in Hong Kong.

177
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,957
Enough with this lecturing!

178
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,180
How dare you?

179
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,380
Oh, did that offend you?

180
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,797
But don't forget,

181
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:42,586
I'm a lot angrier than you are right now
and with a hell of a lot better reason.

182
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:47,860
You can just keep being yourself with
your holier-than-thou attitude, Avdol.

183
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,020
Why, you...

184
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,120
Mr. Joestar!

185
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:52,530
That's enough.

186
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:53,820
Just let him go.

187
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,342
Now that his mind is made up, I
doubt that anybody could stop him.

188
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:03,380
Yeah, I've lost all respect
for him, that's all.

189
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:06,300
My impression of him was completely wrong.

190
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,960
You are correct in that I
did run in fear from him.

191
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:14,339
You see, I'm certain that
Foresight will let us win.

192
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:18,120
Rushing in without thinking
will get us killed. Oh?

193
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:21,460
Then I'll say this with certainty, too.

194
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:25,040
Your precious little
divination will be wrong.

195
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,280
Time to get off.

196
00:11:55,220 --> 00:11:57,161
I'm here to see a friend of mine.

197
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,180
Now get gone, girl.

198
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:02,538
You're on your own.

199
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:05,297
Please make me your wife.

200
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:06,909
I'll do anything you want.

201
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:09,440
My life will belong to you.

202
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:12,331
Just say whatever you wish of me, my love.

203
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,477
Please let me stay with you.

204
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,384
Let me be by your side forever.

205
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,740
Oh, come on now.

206
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,737
Don't be stupid.

207
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,100
You're still only 16.

208
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:23,397
I'm old enough to marry.

209
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,740
I love you.

210
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,920
Listen, I'm just a no-good drifter, baby.

211
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:43,160
I live each day like it's my last, and
one day, the end will come for me. Shh.

212
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:47,640
This is no life for a lady,
and you have royal blood.

213
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:52,700
We can't have a fairytale marriage, no
matter how much we might love each other.

214
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:53,910
Really?

215
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,817
You've never said that before.

216
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,800
You love me? Yeah. Yeah.

217
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,475
You're the only woman I've ever loved.

218
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:03,540
That's just it.

219
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:06,197
It's because I love you
that we can't marry.

220
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,457
I want you to be happy
and have something better.

221
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,069
You understand, don't you?

222
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,880
I know, sweetheart.

223
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:16,258
This breaks my heart just
as much as it breaks yours.

224
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:22,880
But I'll come back to see you and
hold you like this whenever I can.

225
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:25,460
That's enough to make me happy.

226
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:27,630
Okay.

227
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,688
Goodbye, love you, darling.

228
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,600
You know it's bad manners to eavesdrop.

229
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:54,516
You think I spend too much
time on romance, don't you?

230
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:58,297
But when you've got girls like her all
over the world at your beck and call,

231
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:01,260
well, you've always
got an ally, a partner.

232
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:05,620
They'd do anything for me, even
throw away their own lives.

233
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:11,540
You are aware of how I work,
aren't you, Mr. Centerfold?

234
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:17,920
By the way,

235
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,480
about this Silver Chariot's Polnareff,

236
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:24,057
seems that he left the group and
is looking for you on his own.

237
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:30,737
What do you want to do he totally fell
for your plan hook line and sinker hmm?

238
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:32,820
Shall we go and kill him first!

239
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:11,437
Let's go you know between your
hangman and my emperor i have no doubt

240
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:15,900
that we can kill them all no sweat
this will be a hell of a ride!

241
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:01,180
So he really didn't come back after all.

242
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,130
What?

243
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,460
You've seen him?

244
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:32,131
Are you absolutely sure you
saw a man with two right hands?

245
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,130
Where?

246
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,260
I just saw him.

247
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:51,240
I don't understand it.

248
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:55,460
He was just right there.
There! What? There.

249
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:58,019
He was with that man in the street.

250
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:06,400
The gun is mightier than
the sword. Huh? Hmm.

251
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:10,420
Not bad, if I do say
so myself. Wait. What?

252
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:12,347
Who the hell are you, buddy?

253
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:13,890
Hmm.

254
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:15,400
Whole whores.

255
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:17,091
That's what they call me.

256
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,140
I'm a stand user, just like you are.

257
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,828
And my card is the emperor.

258
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:24,713
Lord Dio paid me to get rid of you guys,

259
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:27,537
so say your prayers and
get ready for a beating.

260
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:28,679
Look here, cowboy.

261
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:31,457
I don't give a rat's
ass who you say you are.

262
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:33,940
Where is the man with two right hands?

263
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:35,560
That was pretty rude.

264
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:38,075
You asked who I am, so I answered you.

265
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:39,460
Well, whatever.

266
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,920
I came here with that guy.

267
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:44,820
He's nearby. What?

268
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,100
Where is he?

269
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,977
There's really no point
at all in you asking that.

270
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:52,600
I, Whole Horse, will have the
pleasure of snuffing you out.

271
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:57,040
Arrogant morons like
you always talk trash,

272
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,729
and it always ends up
the other way around.

273
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:02,260
Oh, was that funny?

274
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,520
Lord Dio had you pegged.

275
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:08,517
Polnareff has the fatal habit of
underestimating his opponents.

276
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,497
Beating him into a corpse
won't be any trouble for you.

277
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:14,880
He was exactly right, so
I couldn't help but laugh.

278
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:21,509
If I can't face him until I defeat you,
then that's just what I'll do, chump.

279
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:23,440
Bring it on.

280
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,900
Ever heard of military chess?

281
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:30,517
The tank is stronger than the soldier,
and the tanks are weak against the mines.

282
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,129
See, it's pretty much
the basics of battle.

283
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:37,097
My emperor is stronger than you,
so I thought I'd be a gentleman.

284
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:41,415
I'll let you know my stand's abilities
before we fight, so we're square.

285
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,120
The gun is mightier than the sword.

286
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,560
Such a brilliant quote.

287
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,980
What are you trying to say exactly?

288
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:56,000
That I have a stand that shoots, and a
sword simply can't beat that. So what?

289
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,080
A pea shooter?

290
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,000
Prepare to die.

291
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,480
You underestimated me.

292
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,920
And now, Pawn O 'Ref, you're dead!

293
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:23,360
If I take off my armor, I
can knock down a bullet!

294
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,360
Wait, what the?

295
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,160
That's impossible!

296
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,740
It bypassed my sword!

297
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,020
Oh, crap!

298
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:37,637
The bullet is also my stand, and
underestimating me just cost you your life.

299
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:38,720
Please leave.

300
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,270
Polnareff!

301
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,460
What? Avdol!

302
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:55,997
I've been worried about you,
and now look where you are!

303
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:58,260
Your ego will end you, Polnareff!

304
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:00,740
You're worried about me? Damn you!

305
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,797
You came here to lecture me again?

306
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:05,097
The enemy already knows
everything about you!

307
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:09,474
You said you're a loner, but from now
on, you won't be able to win alone!

308
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:13,320
What bad timing for an
outsider to interfere.

309
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,217
Polnareff, move!

310
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,771
The bullet's coming back!

311
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,680
Go, Matryshids, run!

312
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,000
I'll melt it down!

313
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,400
Damn that, Avdol!

314
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:31,542
He went after Polnareff himself!

315
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,340
Where are you, Mr. Avdol?

316
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:40,476
Polnareff, I have a terrible feeling.

317
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:43,985
Hey, there's a weird
fight going on over there.

318
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:58,680
The plot hole!

319
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:05,020
What the?

320
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:21,860
Mr. Avgol!

321
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,500
Man, today must be my day. Hey!

322
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:30,357
My gun and centerfold's mirror don't do
very well against Avdol's flames, you see.

323
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:33,205
We were sure he'd be our
most formidable enemy.

324
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:34,360
Talk about luck!

325
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:38,060
With him gone, the game is in the bag.

326
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,140
Mr. Avdol!

327
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:47,528
He's just hurt, that's all.

328
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,320
It's just a minor wound, see?

329
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,306
He's going to start speaking.

330
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,402
He'll open his eyes in a moment.

331
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,540
Right, Mr. Avdol? Right?

332
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:59,724
You're going to wake up, right?

333
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:00,750
Mr.

334
00:22:00,833 --> 00:22:02,197
Avdol, you've got to wake up!

335
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,100
No, please! Mr. Avdol!

336
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,200
That seemed awfully easy.

337
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,340
It was too quick.

338
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:27,072
That's what he gets for lecturing people.

339
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:28,180
Look at him now.

340
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:32,260
What did you say, Polnareff? Mr.

341
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:34,080
Avdol was worried about you.

342
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,849
Who asked him for help
because I never did?

343
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:39,557
He likes to meddle in
other people's business,

344
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,934
but he's slow as hell, so they got him.

345
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:45,397
Guys like him just get
in the way and screw up.

346
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,774
That's why I said I was going in alone.

347
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:49,340
You bastard.

348
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:51,480
He saved your life.

349
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:52,760
How dare you?

350
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:06,040
I am sick of it!

351
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:12,440
Having people up and die on me!

352
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:14,910
Polnareff...

353
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:19,280
I'm so sick of it!

354
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:22,260
You hear me?!

355
00:23:39,740 --> 00:23:42,417
All the old paintings on the tomb.

356
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:44,457
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

357
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:46,937
If they move too quick, oh-way-oh!

358
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:49,117
They're falling down like a domino.

359
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,797
All the bars are men by the Nile.

360
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,797
They've got their money on a bet.

361
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,437
Called crocodiles.

362
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:58,397
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

363
00:23:58,480 --> 00:24:00,757
Falling types of the hookah. I say.

364
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,477
Walk

365
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:08,837
like

366
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:09,750
an Egyptian.

367
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:24,397
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

368
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:26,397
Spin around and they cross the floor.

369
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:27,917
They've got the moves.

370
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:31,077
You drop your drink then
they bring you more.

371
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:33,697
All the school kids so sick of books.

372
00:24:33,780 --> 00:24:35,777
They're like the punk and the metal band.

373
00:24:35,860 --> 00:24:37,320
When the buzzer rings.

374
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,017
They're walking like an Egyptian.

375
00:24:40,100 --> 00:24:42,740
All the kids in the marketplace say.

376
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:51,580
Walk like an Egyptian.

377
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:58,237
For such a tough guy, he
sure was easy to finish off.

378
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:01,777
Come to think of it, that sweet sister
of yours was really good at sobbing.

379
00:25:01,860 --> 00:25:04,277
You want me to hold these
regrets inside and run away?

380
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:06,897
Don't let him get to you, you're
much stronger than that Mr.

381
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:07,810
Avdol told you.

382
00:25:07,893 --> 00:25:09,721
He begged you not to fight alone.
